Additional Use Grant: You may make production use of the Licensed Work,
                      provided Your use does not include any of the following:

                      (a) offering the Licensed Work, or a derivative of it, to
                      third parties on a hosted or embedded basis as a
                      competitive offering; or

                      (b) production use by, or on behalf of, a Large
                      Organization after its Free Period has ended.

                      An "affiliate" is any entity that controls, is controlled
                      by, or is under common control with an organization. For
                      the purposes of this definition, "control" means
                      ownership of more than fifty percent of the voting
                      interests of an entity, or the power, direct or indirect,
                      to direct its management.

                      A "Large Organization" is a for-profit organization that
                      has 100 or more individuals working for it or for any of
                      its affiliates as employees or as individual contractors,
                      whether full-time or part-time, each counted once.
                      Non-profit organizations, charities, foundations,
                      educational and healthcare institutions operated on a
                      non-profit basis, and government bodies (other than
                      for-profit enterprises owned by a government) are not
                      Large Organizations.

                      An organization's "Free Period" ends thirty days after
                      the latest of: 1 February 2027; the date on which
                      production use of the Licensed Work is first made by or
                      on behalf of that organization; and the date that
                      organization first becomes a Large Organization.

                      Using an instance operated by another person or
                      organization, to which that person or organization gives
                      You access free of charge, is not production use by You
                      for the purposes of (b), unless that instance is operated
                      wholly or principally for You or was set up at Your
                      request. An instance operated wholly or principally for a
                      Large Organization, or set up at its request, is
                      production use by, and on behalf of, that Large
                      Organization, whatever is charged for access to it.

                      Subject to (b), use within Your organization and its
                      affiliates is within this grant. Hosting or using the
                      Licensed Work for internal purposes within an
                      organization and its affiliates is not a competitive
                      offering.

                      You host an instance when it runs on infrastructure You
                      control. Infrastructure is controlled by the person or
                      organization that rents the server, virtual machine or
                      other computing resource the instance runs on in its own
                      name as the tenant or, if it is not rented, that owns it,
                      even if someone else administers it on its behalf.
                      However, a provider that supplies such resources to a
                      tenant and installs the Licensed Work on them, or offers
                      them with the Licensed Work preinstalled or installable
                      by the provider's own tools, hosts that instance.

                      For the purposes of (a), giving third parties access to
                      an instance You host is a competitive offering when You
                      charge, or anyone acting on Your behalf or under an
                      arrangement with You charges, for that access or for any
                      plugins, capacity, quotas or support for that instance.
                      Subject to (b), offering such access free of charge is
                      permitted, including where You charge only for
                      consulting, process design, configuration, integration
                      development or training, provided those charges are not
                      for access, plugins, capacity, quotas or support for that
                      instance.

                      Installing a separate instance for each customer, on
                      infrastructure that customer controls and that You do not
                      supply, is not a hosted offering.

                      A "competitive offering" is a Product offered to third
                      parties on a paid basis, including through paid support
                      arrangements, that significantly overlaps with the
                      capabilities of the Licensed Work. If Your Product is not
                      a competitive offering when You first make it generally
                      available, it will not become one later because the
                      Licensor releases a new version of the Licensed Work with
                      additional capabilities. Products that are not provided
                      on a paid basis are not competitive.

                      "Product" means software offered to end users to manage
                      in their own environments, or offered as a service on a
                      hosted basis.

                      "Embedded" means including the source code or executable
                      code of the Licensed Work in a Product, or packaging a
                      Product so that the Licensed Work must be downloaded, or
                      must be accessed other than through its network
                      interfaces, for that Product to operate.

                      Interacting with a running instance of the Licensed Work
                      over its network interfaces, such as its REST API or its
                      MCP server, is not embedding, including where a Product
                      cannot operate without such an instance, and does not, by
                      itself, fall outside this grant. This paragraph does not
                      displace (a) or (b): whether giving third parties access
                      to an instance You host, through any of its interfaces,
                      is a competitive offering is determined under (a). A
                      Product that itself downloads, installs or bundles the
                      Licensed Work is Embedded, even if it then interacts with
                      it only over its network interfaces.

                      Subject to (b), installing, configuring, operating,
                      supporting and training on the Licensed Work for a
                      customer, including for a fee, is permitted, provided
                      that each customer receives a separate instance on
                      infrastructure that customer controls and that You do not
                      supply. Operating or supporting that customer's instance
                      on the customer's behalf, including for a fee, does not
                      make it an instance You host and is not a hosted
                      offering.

